  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "can: requests for information (review)",
      "title_form": "Can: pedir información (repaso)",
      "title_target": "Can: requests for information (review)",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos **can** para pedir información o hacer peticiones de forma educada en una tienda. Es un verbo modal: **no cambia** con la persona (I can, you can, he can) y va seguido del **verbo en infinitivo** sin \"to\".\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n- **Can I + verbo...?** → para preguntar (pedir permiso o información).\n- **Can you + verbo...?** → para preguntar a otra persona.\n\n**Ejemplos:**\n\n- `Can I try on this shirt?` = ¿Puedo probarme esta camisa?\n- `Can you help me?` = ¿Puedes ayudarme?\n\n**Respuestas cortas:**\n\n- **Yes, I can.** / **No, I can't.**\n\n**Nota:** En preguntas, el orden es **Can + sujeto + verbo**. No digas \"I can try on?\" como pregunta.",
      "description_md_target": "We use **can** to ask for information or make polite requests in a store. It is a modal verb: it **does not change** with the person (I can, you can, he can) and is followed by the **infinitive verb** without \"to\".\n\n**Structure:**\n\n- **Can I + verb...?** → to ask (for permission or information).\n- **Can you + verb...?** → to ask another person.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n- `Can I try on this shirt?` = Can I try on this shirt?\n- `Can you help me?` = Can you help me?\n\n**Short answers:**\n\n- **Yes, I can.** / **No, I can't.**\n\n**Note:** In questions, the order is **Can + subject + verb**. Do not say \"I can try on?\" as a question.",
      "grammar_structure": "Can + subject + verb (infinitive) + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "can_modal",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Negativo",
          "Pregunta"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "I can try on",
            "I can't try on",
            "Can I try on?"
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "you can try on",
            "you can't try on",
            "Can you try on?"
          ],
          [
            "he/she/it",
            "he can try on",
            "he can't try on",
            "Can he try on?"
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "we can try on",
            "we can't try on",
            "Can we try on?"
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "they can try on",
            "they can't try on",
            "Can they try on?"
          ]
        ]
      },
